<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 206)</h2>
<p><b>Watch a folder for dailies.</b> File ▸ Watch Folder for Dailies… points Asobi at a delivery folder; new renders join the playlist by themselves.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Only once they're finished.</b> Farms write frames one at a time, so a new arrival is believed complete when a <b>done marker</b> appears (<code>SH010_v002.done</code> beside it, or <code>DONE</code> inside a render folder) — or when its writing goes quiet for a few seconds.</li>
<li>Movies, loose frame sequences and render folders each count as one delivery, and a render folder's clip takes the <b>folder's name</b> — the shot name your pipeline gave it.</li>
<li>What's already in the folder when you start watching stays put — watching is for what arrives next, not a re-ingest of history.</li>
</ul>
<p>Also: these release notes are now legible in dark mode — they were black on dark grey.</p>
]]></description>
